   "line": [],
   "spoken": "A moment to break the development rule — when you can just pile up on a target and it works, do it: bring the queen out to f3, and after the forced defence, an in-between pawn thrust to e6 springs a winning fork. Constantly modulating between applying the principles and knowing when to violate them is what makes chess exhilarating.",
   "kind": "tactic",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
